## Results — hold-out test set (n = 200, threshold 0.5)

| Model | CV ROC-AUC (train) | Test ROC-AUC | Test PR-AUC | Recall | Precision | Brier |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| LogisticRegression | 0.769 ± 0.053 | 0.806 | 0.633 | 0.80 | 0.56 | 0.182 |
| **XGBoost** (deployed) | **0.790 ± 0.035** | 0.784 | 0.619 | 0.70 | 0.55 | 0.180 |

XGBoost confusion matrix @ 0.5: TN 106, FP 34, FN 18, TP 42.

**Why XGBoost is deployed despite LR's slightly higher test AUC:** its
cross-validated AUC is higher *and* lower-variance (±0.035 vs ±0.053); the 200-row
test split is small enough that the two models are within noise. XGBoost's tree
structure also lets SHAP's `TreeExplainer` produce **exact** Shapley values in
Phase 2. `recall` here = the share of true defaulters the bank would have denied.

